WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.209
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:06.509 --> 00:00:10.070
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:17.492
Unit six: Mixed Conditionals, Wish and If Only. Today you will talk about regrets and unreal situations.

4
00:00:17.792 --> 00:00:20.468
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:24.701
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:26.389
Wish.

7
00:00:27.383 --> 00:00:29.673
Wish means to want something to be different.

8
00:00:30.283 --> 00:00:31.760
I wish I had a bike.

9
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.584
Your turn. Say: Wish.

10
00:00:37.433 --> 00:00:38.342
Wish.

11
00:00:39.083 --> 00:00:40.096
If only.

12
00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:43.048
If only means a strong wish.

13
00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.417
If only I knew the answer.

14
00:00:46.017 --> 00:00:48.843
Your turn. Say: If only.

15
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.968
If only.

16
00:00:53.717 --> 00:00:54.578
Mixed.

17
00:00:55.583 --> 00:00:57.815
Mixed means combining two types.

18
00:00:58.417 --> 00:01:00.126
This is a mixed conditional.

19
00:01:00.717 --> 00:01:02.765
Your turn. Say: Mixed.

20
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:06.497
Mixed.

21
00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.112
Past.

22
00:01:09.117 --> 00:01:10.977
Past means time before now.

23
00:01:11.583 --> 00:01:13.362
The past cannot change.

24
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:16.684
Your turn. Say: Past.

25
00:01:19.533 --> 00:01:20.372
Past.

26
00:01:21.117 --> 00:01:21.955
Present.

27
00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.578
Present means time now.

28
00:01:25.183 --> 00:01:26.730
This affects the present.

29
00:01:27.317 --> 00:01:29.354
Your turn. Say: Present.

30
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:32.922
Present.

31
00:01:33.683 --> 00:01:34.859
Opportunity.

32
00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:38.093
Opportunity means a good chance.

33
00:01:38.683 --> 00:01:40.137
I missed the opportunity.

34
00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:43.716
Your turn. Say: Opportunity.

35
00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:47.661
Opportunity.

36
00:01:48.417 --> 00:01:49.464
Mistake.

37
00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:52.113
Mistake means something wrong.

38
00:01:52.717 --> 00:01:53.938
It was a mistake.

39
00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:56.900
Your turn. Say: Mistake.

40
00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:00.617
Mistake.

41
00:02:01.383 --> 00:02:02.779
Apologise.

42
00:02:03.783 --> 00:02:05.853
Apologise means to say sorry.

43
00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.275
I apologise for the delay.

44
00:02:08.883 --> 00:02:11.791
Your turn. Say: Apologise.

45
00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:15.785
Apologise.

46
00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:20.274
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.117 --> 00:02:23.186
Visal, how do I use wish?

48
00:02:24.283 --> 00:02:35.341
Wish plus the past simple shows a present regret: I wish I had more time. Wish plus the past perfect shows a past regret: I wish I had listened.

49
00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:38.090
What is a mixed conditional?

50
00:02:39.183 --> 00:02:49.373
It joins a past condition with a present result. If I had studied medicine, I would be a doctor now. The if clause is past perfect and the result uses would.

51
00:02:50.483 --> 00:02:52.262
Can I use were with I?

52
00:02:53.350 --> 00:03:04.596
Yes. In formal English we say If I were you, I would apologise, and I wish I were taller. Were is used for all persons in unreal sentences.

53
00:03:05.733 --> 00:03:07.373
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:08.217 --> 00:03:13.339
Grammar focus: wish plus past; if only plus past perfect.

55
00:03:13.639 --> 00:03:14.931
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:15.617 --> 00:03:17.082
I wish I had more time.

57
00:03:17.983 --> 00:03:21.028
If I had studied medicine, I would be a doctor now.

58
00:03:21.967 --> 00:03:29.623
Use wish plus the past simple for a present regret and the past perfect for a past regret. In unreal sentences use were for all persons.

59
00:03:30.383 --> 00:03:33.941
Be careful! Don't say: I wish I have more time.

60
00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.503
Say: I wish I had more time.

61
00:03:38.803 --> 00:03:40.443
Wish + past.

62
00:03:41.233 --> 00:03:43.874
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:45.737
A Regret.

64
00:03:46.037 --> 00:03:47.840
Vichea missed the bus this morning.

65
00:03:48.833 --> 00:03:50.844
He wishes he had left home earlier.

66
00:03:51.833 --> 00:03:54.495
If he had caught the bus, he would be at school now.

67
00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.650
If only he were more organised.

68
00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:01.084
Now he promises to set two alarms.

69
00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:06.446
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:07.283 --> 00:04:09.736
Present regret: I wish I blank more time.

71
00:04:10.036 --> 00:04:13.318
A, had. B, have. C, will have.

72
00:04:16.867 --> 00:04:18.448
The answer is A: had.

73
00:04:19.583 --> 00:04:22.036
Past regret: I wish I blank listened.

74
00:04:22.336 --> 00:04:25.327
A, would. B, had. C, have.

75
00:04:28.867 --> 00:04:30.588
The answer is B: had.

76
00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.005
If I blank you, I would apologise.

77
00:04:34.305 --> 00:04:37.030
A, am. B, be. C, were.

78
00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:42.125
The answer is C: were.

79
00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:45.817
A mixed conditional links blank and present.

80
00:04:46.117 --> 00:04:49.724
A, past. B, future. C, never.

81
00:04:53.267 --> 00:04:55.510
The answer is A: past.

82
00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:58.115
What does Vichea promise?

83
00:04:58.415 --> 00:05:02.638
A, a holiday. B, two alarms. C, a new bus.

84
00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.501
The answer is B: two alarms.

85
00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:12.852
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:13.717 --> 00:05:14.927
What do you wish?

87
00:05:23.717 --> 00:05:25.078
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:25.378 --> 00:05:34.732
I wish I had more time to practise English. If I had started earlier, I would speak better now. I will study every day from now on.

89
00:05:35.032 --> 00:05:36.752
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:43.333
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and wish plus past; if only plus past perfect.

91
00:05:43.633 --> 00:05:48.827
Today's value is reflective awareness. Notice your own experience with care and honesty.

92
00:05:49.127 --> 00:05:51.397
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

93
00:05:51.697 --> 00:05:54.303
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

